er/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded" "basis" 335 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+10\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${2}^{2},$ writing the constant term $10$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{2}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y-2{)}^{2}-{2}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y-2{)}^{2}+6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded" "basis" 335 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3e2580e130e3316029db96b76a6dfc8a419f7b6adb869cfc483893db3d8a4e12" "basis" 335 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-141612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded" "basis" 335