"category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-141612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3e2580e130e3316029db96b76a6dfc8a419f7b6adb869cfc483893db3d8a4e12"} {"question" "q-141612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-141612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y-2{)}^{2}+3"] ["math" "(y-2{)}^{2}+6"] ["math" "(y-2{)}^{2}-4"] ["math" "(y-4{)}^{2}+1"] ["math" "(y-4{)}^{2}+5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-141612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y-2{)}^{2}+6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-235868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Rewrite the following expression as the sum of a perfect square and a constant.\n\n$({x}^{2}-8x+16)+5=(${{field-1}}${)}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-235868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2ax+{a}^{2}=(x-a{)}^{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+16 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2} & = \\\\ (x-4{)}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-8x+16)+5 & = \\\\ (x-4{)}^{2}+5 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-235868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3e2580e130e3316029db96b76a6dfc8a419f7b6adb869cfc483893db3d8a4e12"} {"question" "q-235868" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-235868" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-235868" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-235868" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-250517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the expression ${x}^{2}-10x$ is written as $(x-p{)}^{2}+q$, then what are the values of $p$ and $q?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-250517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+0\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${5}^{2},$ writing the constant term $0$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{5}^{2}+0\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2}+0\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-5{)}^{2}-25\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=5$ and $q=-25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/state.json" "file_sha256" "927e24c36de12d5d49faeb08b3fd06aec2b9c2c141da2409514d8598e99d9ded"} {"question" "q-250517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3e2580e130e3316029db96b76a6dfc8a419f7b6adb869cfc483893db3d8a4e12"} {"question" "q-250517" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-